From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 09:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lower hipBLASLt preferred architecture ROCm gate

PyTorch 2.14.0 already prefers hipBLASLt on gfx1100, gfx1101, and
gfx1151 starting with ROCm 7.13. Lower that gate to ROCm 7.2, which is
the version shipped by openRuyi and avoids rocBLAS fp16 GEMM failures
on gfx1100 for some problem shapes.

Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/10a5f2ff7c90d8c84938b0e789ab2f4145f90b5d
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [distribution-specific ROCm version gate]
---
 aten/src/ATen/cuda/detail/CUDAHooks.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aten/src/ATen/cuda/detail/CUDAHooks.cpp b/aten/src/ATen/cuda/detail/CUDAHooks.cpp
--- a/aten/src/ATen/cuda/detail/CUDAHooks.cpp
+++ b/aten/src/ATen/cuda/detail/CUDAHooks.cpp
@@ -556,7 +556,7 @@ const std::vector<std::string>& CUDAHooks::getHipblasltPreferredArchs() const {
 #if ROCM_VERSION >= 70000
     "gfx950",
 #endif
-#if ROCM_VERSION >= 71300
+#if ROCM_VERSION >= 70200
     "gfx1100", "gfx1101", "gfx1151",
 #endif
 #if ROCM_VERSION >= 71400
